       41  '''Căușeni District''' ({{langx|ro|Raionul Căușeni}}, {{IPAc-ro|pron|C|ă|.|u|'|ș|e|ni}}) is a district in the central part of [[Moldova]], with the administrative center at [[Căușeni]]. The other major city in the district is [[Căinari]]. According to the [[2024 Moldovan census]], the population of 
       42  ==History==
       43  The [[Căușeni]] District was the first district of Moldova to be recorded in 1455. The next localities of the region to be recorded were: [[Zaim, Căușeni|Zaim]], [[Cîrnățeni]], [[Fîrlădeni, Căușeni|Fîrlădeni]], but not until the period 1535–1573. In the 16th-18th centuries, intensive agriculture and
       44  ==Geography==
       45  Căușeni District is located in the southern part of Moldova. It is bordered by the following districts: [[Ialoveni District|Ialoveni]] and [[Anenii Noi District|Anenii Noi]] in the north, [[Slobozia District]] in the east, [[Ștefan Vodă District]] in the south-east, bordering in the south with [[Ukr
       46  ===Climate===
       47  The district has a [[continental climate]] with an annual average district temperature of {{convert|11|C|0}}. The July average temperature is {{convert|23|C|0}}, and in January it is {{convert|-4|C|0}}. Annual precipitation 450–550 mm. Average wind speed is 2–5 metres/second.
       48  ===Fauna===
       49  Typical European fauna, with the presence of such mammals such as [[fox]]es, [[hedgehog]]s, [[deer]], [[wild boar]], [[European polecat|polecat]], [[Lynx|wild cat]], [[Stoat|ermine]]. and others. Of birds there are: [[partridge]]s, [[crow]]s, [[eagle]]s, [[starling]]s, [[swallow]]s, and more.
       50  ===Flora===
       51  Forests of the district are composed of tree species such as [[oak]], [[Ash (Fraxinus)|ash]], [[hornbeam]], [[Silver linden|linden]], [[maple]], [[walnut]] and others. Other common plants are: [[Artemisia (plant)|wormwood]], [[knotweed]], [[fescue]], and [[Urtica|nettle]].
       52  ===Rivers===
       53  Căușeni district is located in the [[Dniester|Dniester River]] basin, whose main tributary is the [[Botna|Botna River]] (152 km). Most lakes are artificial in origin.
