      123  == Economy{{Citation needed|reason=Not in 2024 Census Data|date=February 2026}} ==
      124  The main economic activities of the district are agriculture and manufacturing. Currently there are 15,721 registered companies in the district. The different types of manufacturing that predominate are: wine-making, processing of milk, bakery products, and other industries based on local [[raw mate
      125  == Education{{Citation needed|reason=Not in 2024 Census Data|date=February 2026}} ==
      126  The district operates 69 educational institutions, including institutions of [[secondary education]] - 37 (14,960 students), [[kindergartens]] - 31 (3014 children), a creative center for children.
      127  ==Politics==
      128  {{Update|date=February 2026}}
      129  Căușeni District has historically voted mainly for [[Centre-right|right-wing parties]]. In Moldova the district is represented by the [[Alliance for European Integration]] (AEI). The [[Party of Communists of the Republic of Moldova]] (PCRM) has seen a continuous fall in the percentage of the vote du
      130  During the last three elections the vote for the [[Alliance for European Integration|AEI]] has grown from 11,179 votes to 20,140 votes representing an increase of 80%.
